---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How the NeuroGIDAS website is built to be usable by everyone, and how to tell us if something doesn't work for you."
  updated="October 20, 2026"
  summary={[
    'We want everyone to be able to use this site, including people who use screen readers, keyboards, or zoom.',
    'We aim to meet the WCAG 2.2 Level AA guidelines.',
    'If something doesn’t work for you, email us and we will fix it.',
  ]}
>
  <h2>Our goal</h2>
  <p>
    NeuroGIDAS is for every student at Eastview, so this website should work for everyone too. We aim to meet the Web Content
    Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA.
  </p>

  <h2>What we’ve done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page can be used with just a keyboard, and there’s a “Skip to content” link at the top.</li>
    <li>Text and buttons have strong color contrast, and color is never the only way information is shown.</li>
    <li>Images and figures have text descriptions for screen readers.</li>
    <li>The site works when you zoom in and on phones, tablets, and computers.</li>
    <li>If your device is set to reduce motion, the site turns its animations off.</li>
    <li>Pages use proper headings so screen readers can jump around easily.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>
    Some links go to outside websites, like research databases and social media. We can’t control how accessible those sites
    are.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If anything on this site is hard to use, email <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>. Tell us which page and
    what went wrong, and we will work on a fix. We can also send you any information from the site in another format.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
